=======================================================================
 test_poisson_2d_shapes - 2D point set and mesh checks on simple shapes
=======================================================================

WHAT THIS IS

  Tests of the 2D Poisson disk sampler in LaGriT,

      createpts / poisson_disk / 2d_polygon / ...

  on convex polygons: a square, a hexagon, a circle and two ellipses.
  Each test checks that the sampled points stay inside the polygon and
  that the mesh built from them is valid, and MEASURES how the points
  are spaced and how good the triangles are.

  There are no reference output files. The checks are properties any
  correct result must have, and the measurements are reported so that
  a change in the sampler shows up as a change in the numbers.

QUICK START

  ./run_poisson_2d_tests.sh  [path-to-lagrit]

  then open, in a web browser,

      logs/summary.html

  That one page has the results table and, for every test, its notes,
  the full measurement report and a picture.

  Requires: LaGriT, Python 3 (standard library only), a POSIX shell.

